<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26679" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lindus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-os</span></b> ), i, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λίνδος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a town in the island of Rhodes, founded by
				Lindus, brother of Ialysus, with a temple of Minerva</i>, now
				<i>Lindo</i>, <i><span class="en">Mel. 2, 7,
			4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 5, 31, 36, § 132</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. N. D.
				3, 21, 54</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lindĭus</span></b> , a,
				um, <i>adj., of</i> or <i>belonging to Lindus, Lindian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lindia Minerva,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					33, 12, 55, § 155</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Chares,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					34, 7, 18, § 41</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cleobulus,</span>”
				<i>of Lindus, one of the seven wise men</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Aus. Sept. Sap. 1, 16</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
